 ### Next action
 Audit each CLI entry point for preflight enforcement, then propose a staged adoption plan for the remaining repositories.
+
+## Viking VFS Phase 3.0 contract closure and client scaffold (2026-08-30)
+
+### Completed work
+- Closed the MCP boundary gaps for standard `resources/list`, numeric JSON-RPC errors, canonical URI handling, and snapshot-pinned batch reads.
+- Added `viking/readBatch` with 32-item and aggregate-byte limits plus per-item error isolation.
+- Extended `stat` and `list` to expose tier availability, freshness, hashes, and inline L0 abstracts without leaking physical paths.
+- Scaffolded the dependency-free ESM package `@toolforge/viking-client` with URI validation, stdio transport, error normalization, metadata-only telemetry, batch reads, and severity-aware tier resolution.
+- Implemented P0/P1 stale-L1 escalation to L2, P2-P4 stale warning behavior, and transparent L1-unavailable fallback to L2.
+- Added the root `test:viking` gate for MCP and client conformance tests.
+
+### Decisions
+- Keep the wire contract at Viking VFS contract version 1.1.0 and advertise server version 0.2.0.
+- Preserve standard MCP methods for interoperability and use `viking/*` extensions only for tier-specific operations.
+- Count batch reads as one RPC while retaining per-resource tier and fallback telemetry; telemetry sinks receive metadata, never resource contents.
+- Defer harness integration and publication-grade benchmarking until the client contract is consumed by both target harnesses.
+
+### Verification
+- `npm run test:viking`: 31 passed, 0 failed.
+- Repository `npm test`: 226 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped.
+- `git diff --check` and Node syntax checks passed.
+- The stdio integration test initialized a real Viking MCP subprocess and completed a snapshot-backed L2 read.
+
+### Remaining work
+- Integrate `@toolforge/viking-client` with `modules/trm-devops/src/core/viking-resolver.ts` and `kb-sync/src/vfs/viking-bridge.ts`.
+- Implement the five-scenario dual-mode benchmark and daily status delta emission.
+- Validate token accounting against the selected production model tokenizer and publish results only after identical-input and repeated-run controls pass.
+
+### Next action
+Integrate the client into `@toolforge/trm-devops` first, preserving raw recursive loading as the benchmark control path, then add `kb-sync` AST-skeleton escalation before full L2 reads.
